  "subtitle": "Scottish shortbread rounds sandwiched with jam and iced",
  "excerpt": "Imperial biscuits are a traditional Scottish biscuit: a pair of crisp, buttery shortbread-style rounds sandwiched together with raspberry jam, then iced on top with a flat white glacé icing and decorated with a small blob of jam in the centre. They are sold in every Scottish bakery and have been a staple of the tea-table since at least the early 20th century. Simple to make, they keep well in a tin.",
