  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Imperial biscuits are a simple bake: a buttery biscuit dough cut into rounds, sandwiched with raspberry jam, and finished with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "glace-icing"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "glacé icing"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The dough is held together by egg yolk rather than a whole egg, which keeps the texture short and crisp. Roll the dough cold and work quickly; soft dough will stick to the cutter and rounds will lose their shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 250,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Biscuit dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Biscuit dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cold, cut into cubes",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Biscuit dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "egg-yolks",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "large",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Biscuit dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vanilla-extract",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Biscuit dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "raspberry-jam",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "seedless",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Filling and icing"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "icing-sugar",
              "amount": 180,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "sifted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Filling and icing"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lemon-juice",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Filling and icing"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the dough"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rub {{unsalted-butter}} into {{plain-flour}} and {{caster-sugar}} until the mixture resembles fine breadcrumbs. Add {{egg-yolks}} and {{vanilla-extract}} and mix to a smooth dough. If it feels crumbly, press it firmly together; do not add water. Flatten into a disc, wrap, and refrigerate for 30 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Roll and cut"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 170°C (conventional). Line two baking trays. Roll the chilled dough on a lightly floured surface to 4 mm thickness. Cut into 5 cm rounds; you need an even number. Re-roll the trimmings and cut again. Place on the lined trays and bake for 12 to 14 minutes until very pale golden at the edges. The tops should remain almost white. Cool on a wire rack for 30 minutes until firm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sandwich and ice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spread a thin layer of {{raspberry-jam}} on the flat side of half the biscuits, then press a second biscuit on top, flat-side down. Mix {{icing-sugar}} with {{lemon-juice}} and just enough water (about 1 to 2 teaspoons added drop by drop) to make a smooth, spreadable icing that holds a ribbon for 2 seconds before dissolving. Spoon a teaspoon of icing onto the top of each sandwiched biscuit and spread to the edges. Add a small dot of jam in the centre before the icing sets. Leave for 30 minutes until the icing is firm."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
